maria: Heads-up — opened a docs PR to add a short 'prompt trimming' troubleshooting guide + tiny SDK examples for handling context-limit failures and graceful fallbacks. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/234 :eyes:

alex: Nice. Can you paste the JS snippet inline so reviewers can quickly scan?

maria: Sure — copied from the PR (keeps it intentionally compact):
```javascript
// trimToFit(prompt, maxTokens) - naive example to drop oldest history
function trimToFit(prompt, maxTokens) {
  if (prompt.length <= maxTokens) return prompt;
  return prompt.slice(-maxTokens);
}

async function generate(client, prompt) {
  let p = prompt;
  for (let attempt = 0; attempt < 3; attempt++) {
    try {
      return await client.generate({ model: 'redwood-1', input: p });
    } catch (e) {
      // handle rate limits with backoff
      if (e.code === 429) {
        await sleep(1000 * Math.pow(2, attempt));
        continue;
      }
      // simple context-error detection (depends on runtime error shape)
      if (e.message && e.message.includes('context length')) {
        // drop older turns and retry
        p = trimToFit(p, 1024);
        continue;
      }
      throw e;
    }
  }
  // final fallback: smaller model with aggressive trimming
  return client.generate({ model: 'redwood-1-small', input: trimToFit(prompt, 800) });
}
```

ben: I like it. Could we also add a minimal console routing example so customers see how to wire a fallback at the platform level? Tiny YAML so it looks familiar.

maria: Added a short routing snippet in the PR notes:
```yaml
routes:
  - match: /v1/generate
    policy:
      - prefer: redwood-1
      - on_capacity: fallback: redwood-1-small
      - on_429: retry: 3
```

jordan: Keep it focused — maybe one runtime snippet (JS) + one platform snippet (YAML). Avoid duplicating Python unless someone asks. Also add a short 'how to repro' section (send a long thread + tiny max_tokens) so QA can validate.

sophie: I'll take review tonight. Suggest we add a very short note about token counting libraries (tiktoken or internal util) and link to the 'context-window' doc page for details. Also add a one-liner about observability: include route + model in logs so ops can correlate 429 spikes to model variants.

maria: Good call. Added a link to the token-counting util and a note about logging. Kept examples terse per feedback.

